#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495095 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096706 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c990d69-54da-5541-948f-0d5eff96feb5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the X-Intercepts of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39666ba2-d1b2-597c-b370-bacf043984d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494437} {:answer/id #uuid "88a7cf58-d916-590f-9785-5e3e2335fcc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494621} {:answer/id #uuid "91de9c2e-7046-525e-8743-3f166f6387d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494649} {:answer/id #uuid "bef9eaf4-0153-5684-97cd-4baabb718807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494765} {:answer/id #uuid "f4fccee5-efce-59e3-b554-79d8ba6b664a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39666ba2-d1b2-597c-b370-bacf043984d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494437} :answer-field/id #uuid "f352a4e4-ace7-5237-beb9-55b20b2b14aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67e144f2-2a3f-5e5b-9938-978ba91cf547" :question/math-academy-id "q-14160" :question/problem "![](images/2a/2a195992bbda673f38856ee5b5ea6f0f14f6cf1303df200d0125e29f365a51e3.png)\n\nWhat is the $x$-intercept of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(1,-2)$ and passes through the point $(5,2).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(1,-2)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y+2)^{2}=4p(x-1).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(5,2),$ we substitute $x=5$ and $y=2$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2+2)^{2} & =4p(5-1) \\\\ 16 & =4p(4) \\\\ p & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+2)^{2} & =4(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola  and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+2)^{2} & =4(x-1) \\\\ 4 & =4(x-1) \\\\ 1 & =x-1 \\\\ x & =1+1 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096706 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c990d69-54da-5541-948f-0d5eff96feb5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the X-Intercepts of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adec1f59-4414-5eba-a9d0-0be0539bcf76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adec1f59-4414-5eba-a9d0-0be0539bcf76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289184} :answer-field/id #uuid "12a4955b-1b39-5914-8df2-241e9e148d62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b992bd0f-c103-5e7d-8240-431930cfc4f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-240666" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d4c21d6ce09ff32004a28d18d223fef7858c377bccb0eb532cf2dda29a545f5e.png)\n\nThe value of the $x$-intercept of the parabola shown above is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-7,-2)$ and passes through the point $(-11,-6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-7,-2)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y+2)^{2}=4p(x+7).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-11,-6),$ we substitute $x=-11$ and $y=-6$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-6+2)^{2} & =4p(-11+7) \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p\\cdot (-4) \\\\ 16 & =-16p \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+2)^{2} & =-4(x+7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+2)^{2} & =-4(x+7) \\\\ 4 & =-4(x+7) \\\\ -1 & =x+7 \\\\ x & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $-8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096708 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e182f71-db24-5c29-9c8b-2fc4b5ab5dd8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Y-Intercepts of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a6a9d26-433a-5092-af7f-f5759c6b0c0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a6a9d26-433a-5092-af7f-f5759c6b0c0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494670} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c9e3b73-c2d8-584a-94b4-ea5f381f00cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d42d975f-c622-5e1c-8f09-860b1ab55e6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-251808" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8f138ed24e1fa76264b344faf3d1a91082b5d0ecc76b66f069939c358176438f.png)\n\nThe value of the $y$-intercept of the parabola shown above  is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(4,5)$ and passes through the point $(6,3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(4,5)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(x-4)^{2}=4p(y-5).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(6,3),$ we substitute $x=6$ and $y=3$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6-4)^{2} & =4p(3-5) \\\\ 4 & =4p(-2) \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2} & =-2(y-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-4)^{2} & =-2(y-5) \\\\ 16 & =-2(y-5) \\\\ -8 & =y-5 \\\\ y & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096708 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e182f71-db24-5c29-9c8b-2fc4b5ab5dd8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Y-Intercepts of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b11eb3e0-5429-5dbf-9eb9-2fe0147cd44a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b11eb3e0-5429-5dbf-9eb9-2fe0147cd44a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291404} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7824f56-f0d4-5e6a-aab1-6508db9a964a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ccfe5a9-f5ef-5f9b-aef4-c87ce64bd0db" :question/math-academy-id "q-251810" :question/problem "![](images/31/31618ee78ebe4834cf76aedebce7c25eca8413c6a4b9d91761ccc38dbd32b01d.png)\n\nThe value of the $y$-intercept of the parabola shown above  is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(2,2)$ and passes through the point $(-2,-2).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(2,2)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}=4p(y-2).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-2,-2),$ we substitute $x=-2$ and $y=-2$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2-2)^{2} & =4p(-2-2) \\\\ 16 & =4p(-4) \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =-4(y-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-2)^{2} & =-4(y-2) \\\\ 4 & =-4(y-2) \\\\ -1 & =y-2 \\\\ y & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096706 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c990d69-54da-5541-948f-0d5eff96feb5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the X-Intercepts of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16a63b0f-5612-5697-9957-612d1afe2968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494361} {:answer/id #uuid "4e986982-9ed8-549e-8c70-12068b401fa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494477} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd1f648-8d54-565c-aea2-285561a08bbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494761} {:answer/id #uuid "e0b6c92a-bb8f-5e61-895e-e5d4cb68972d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494850} {:answer/id #uuid "eb93ffdc-f3a1-5a8a-add9-8b3ab4687a54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb93ffdc-f3a1-5a8a-add9-8b3ab4687a54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494877} :answer-field/id #uuid "442e0f0e-7158-585e-a6f1-74b91f5e78ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da7d6a02-447c-52f1-87f8-add9a2f9923e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73835" :question/problem "![](images/89/8965c5f1d97491db6ab606adf083d0d19d1a5812e7cd8060019b8253e9b726cd.png)\n\nWhat is the $x$-intercept of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-2,2)$ and passes through the point $(7,5).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-2,2)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y-2)^{2}=4p(x+2).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(7,5),$ we substitute $x=7$ and $y=5$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-2)^{2} & =4p(7+2) \\\\ 9 & =4p(9) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-2)^{2} & =(x+2) \\\\ 4 & =x+2 \\\\ x & =4-2 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $2.$"}]}
